.TH DEEDEE 1 "September 2026" "Dee Dee" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
deedee \- conversational technical reviewer, mentor, and project assistant

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python chatbot.py

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Dee Dee
is a conversational chatbot with structured memory, intent detection,
adaptive conversational tone, a command system, and scoped community
authorization.

Dee Dee can remember a user's name and task context, respond to common
questions, tell jokes, recognize different ways of expressing an intent,
and adapt replies according to conversational context.

Her normal personality is technical, strict, dry, sarcastic, ironic,
and deliberately old-school in presentation.

Sarcasm is reduced when the conversation indicates genuine discouragement
or a serious personal context. Repeated technical failures may cause Dee Dee
to move from focused troubleshooting into a more motivational tone.

.SH STARTING DEE DEE
From the project directory, run:

.PP
.nf
python chatbot.py
.fi

.PP
The terminal prompt is:

.PP
.nf
U:
.fi

.PP
Enter normal conversational text or a command beginning with
.BR ! .

.SH CONVERSATION
Dee Dee understands several classes of conversational input.

.TP
.B Greetings and goodbyes
Common greetings and natural goodbyes are recognized in English and
Argentine Spanish.

.TP
.B Common questions
Questions such as "who are you?" and "what can you do?" receive
direct responses.

.TP
.B Name memory
A user may introduce a name with phrases such as:

.PP
.nf
my name is Darko
me llamo Darko
.fi

.PP
The stored name can later be recalled conversationally.

.TP
.B Task memory
Dee Dee can remember a current activity, its focus, and a next step.

.TP
.B Context
Short replies may be interpreted according to the previous question or
conversation state.

.TP
.B Jokes
Jokes can be requested conversationally or with
.BR !joke .

.TP
.B Adaptive tone
Dee Dee may respond in focused, playful, sarcastic, serious, or
motivational ways according to the current conversation.

.SH COMMANDS
Command names are case-insensitive.

.SS General commands

.TP
.B !help
Display the command registry.

.TP
.B !motd
Display the service message of the day.

.TP
.B !version
Display version information for the active bot components.

.TP
.B !uptime
Display process uptime.

.TP
.B !identity
Display the stable adapter identity and current authorization scope.

.TP
.B !whois [id]
Display the current user's profile information, or authorized identity
information for another user.

.TP
.B !joke
Return a randomized Dee Dee joke.

.TP
.B !mood
Display Dee Dee's current adaptively inferred conversational tone.
This command reports the tone; it does not set it.

.TP
.B !exit
Close the current Dee Dee session.

.SS Authorization and community commands

.TP
.B !role [id]
Display a user's effective role.

.TP
.B !role set <id> <role>
Assign a role when the caller has sufficient authority.

.TP
.B !flag [id]
Display service flags.

.TP
.B !flag add <id> <flag>
Add a service flag when authorized.

.TP
.B !flag remove <id> <flag>
Remove a service flag when authorized.

.TP
.B !capabilities [id]
Display effective capabilities.

.TP
.B !users
List identities visible in the current authorization scope.

.TP
.B !audit [count]
Display recent authority-change audit entries.
Access is restricted.

.TP
.B !founder
Display the active Founder identity.

.TP
.B !founder transfer <id> CONFIRM
Transfer root authority to another known identity.
Explicit confirmation is required.

.TP
.B !scope
Display the current authorization scope.

.TP
.B !authz <capability> [scope]
Explain whether the current identity is authorized for a capability.

.TP
.B !policy <capability>
Display policy information for a capability when authorized.

.TP
.B !shutdown
Request service shutdown.
This operation is restricted to the Founder.

.SH ROLES
Dee Dee recognizes the following authority roles:

.TP
.B FOUNDER
Root service authority.

.TP
.B SOP
Highest delegated service authority.

.TP
.B OP
Operational and community-administration authority.

.TP
.B DV
Developer and technical-review authority.

.TP
.B MB
Normal member authority.

.TP
.B GT
Guest authority.

.PP
Higher rank does not imply that technical evidence becomes correct.
Authorization controls permitted operations, not technical truth.

.SH FLAGS
Service flags are separate from roles.

.TP
.B T
Trusted.

.TP
.B R
Reviewer.

.TP
.B M
Mentor.

.TP
.B C
Contributor.

.PP
A flag does not automatically make a user an operator or administrator.

.SH SCOPES
Authorization may be evaluated within one of these scopes:

.TP
.B SELF
The current stable identity.

.TP
.B CHANNEL
A particular channel.

.TP
.B GUILD
A particular server or community.

.TP
.B GLOBAL
The Dee Dee service as a whole.

.PP
Community roles may be scoped so that authority in one guild does not
automatically apply in another.

.SH DISCORD IDENTITIES
When used with a Discord adapter, authorization is based on stable numeric
Discord user IDs rather than display names or nicknames.

Display-name changes therefore do not change authorization identity.

Guild and channel identifiers are likewise used to construct the applicable
authorization scope.

.SH EXAMPLES
Start Dee Dee:

.PP
.nf
python chatbot.py
.fi

.PP
Ask about Dee Dee:

.PP
.nf
U: who are you?
U: what can you do?
.fi

.PP
Use conversational memory:

.PP
.nf
U: my name is Darko
U: what is my name?
.fi

.PP
Ask for a joke:

.PP
.nf
U: tell me a joke
U: !joke
.fi

.PP
Inspect the current tone:

.PP
.nf
U: !mood
.fi

.PP
List commands:

.PP
.nf
U: !help
.fi

.SH NATIVE COMMAND BACKEND
Dee Dee can optionally use a small native C backend for ASCII command-name
validation and lowercasing.

.PP
Build the native backend from the project directory with:

.PP
.nf
./tools/build-native.sh
.fi

.PP
The generated shared library is stored under
.BR build/ ,
which is not tracked by Git.

.PP
If the native shared library is unavailable, Dee Dee automatically uses an
equivalent Python implementation. Command syntax and registry behavior remain
owned by the Python command layer.

.SH NOTES
Conversation memory and authorization state are separate concepts.

Commands that inspect or modify another identity may require additional
authorization.

Empty or whitespace-only conversational input produces no conversational
response.

